            },
            "kind": "REWORK",
            "comments": [
                {
                    "file": "yaml/xyz/openbmc_project/Inventory/Item/NetworkInterface.interface.yaml",
                    "line": 18,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Patrick Williams",
                        "email": "patrick@stwcx.xyz",
                        "username": "williamspatrick"
                    },
                    "message": "What is the difference between \"exposed\" \"produced\" \"contained\" and any other verbs we already use?"
                },
                {
                    "file": "yaml/xyz/openbmc_project/Inventory/Item/NetworkInterface.interface.yaml",
                    "line": 18,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Eric Liu",
                        "email": "liuer@nvidia.com",
                        "username": "liuer-sys"
                    },
                    "message": "Thanks for the question. `exposed_by` / `exposing` follows the\nexisting PDI convention used between PCIeFunction and PCIeDevice\n[1][2]: a logical function and the physical device that exposes\nit.\n\nSome context on the related verbs:\n\n- `produced_by` / `producing`: the producer creates the function\n  (e.g., a PCIe function produces this network function).\n- `contained_by` / `containing`: physical containment (e.g., a\n  chassis containing items).\n- `exposed_by` / `exposing`: a physical device exposes a logical\n  function -- the case we have here for NetworkAdapter and\n  NetworkInterface.\n\nPlease let me know if a different verb is preferred and I will\nupdate accordingly. Thanks.\n\n[1] yaml/xyz/openbmc_project/Inventory/Item/PCIeFunction.interface.yaml\n[2] yaml/xyz/openbmc_project/Inventory/Item/PCIeDevice.interface.yaml"
                },
                {
                    "file": "yaml/xyz/openbmc_project/Inventory/Item/NetworkInterface.interface.yaml",
                    "line": 27,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Patrick Williams",
                        "email": "patrick@stwcx.xyz",
                        "username": "williamspatrick"
                    },
                    "message": "Please read requirements.md for naming conventions on associations."
                },
                {
                    "file": "yaml/xyz/openbmc_project/Inventory/Item/NetworkInterface.interface.yaml",
                    "line": 27,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Eric Liu",
                        "email": "liuer@nvidia.com",
                        "username": "liuer-sys"
                    },
                    "message": "Thanks for the pointer. Renamed in PS3 to follow requirements.md:\n\n- `assignable_physical_network_ports` -> `assigned_to`\n- `assigned_network_device_function` -> `assigning`\n\nSentence test:\n- NetworkInterface is `assigned_to` the Port.\n- Port is `assigning` the NetworkInterface.\n\nFor context, the existing `connecting` / `connected_to` uses in\nPDI describe physical hardware connections (FabricAdapter,\nNetworkAdapter, Cpu, Cable, PCIeSwitch, etc.). Since\nNetworkInterface is a logical MAC/function rather than a physical\nentity, a new participle pair seemed clearer than reusing\n`connecting` here.\n\nPlease let me know if different naming is preferred and I will\nupdate accordingly. Thanks."
                }
            ],
